{"kind":"request","text":"Close dynamic client registration by default\n\nScope: ruling on 5d56adca. O4 runs with no dynamic registration, and\nlater Workers turn it on only behind a rate limit.\n\nAdd OAUTH_DYNAMIC_REGISTRATION, a deployment setting, off by default.\nWhen off, POST /oauth/register refuses with a fixed RFC 7591 error\nand writes nothing, and the authorization-server metadata omits\nregistration_endpoint. When it is exactly \"on\", today's behavior holds.\nAny other value closes the OAuth routes, as other invalid OAuth\nsettings do. Metadata-document clients keep working in both states.\n\nDone when tests show both states, the metadata change, a refused\nregistration that writes no row, a metadata-document client still\ncompleting the code flow with registration off, and an invalid value\nclosing the routes, with a frozen gate, the checker's review, and the\nhead on main. Document the setting in docs/mcp.md and\ndocs/security/settings.md.\n\nOrder: next, before O4's Worker deploys.","body":{"conditions":"OAUTH_DYNAMIC_REGISTRATION defaults off, an off Worker refuses registration without a write and omits registration_endpoint, metadata-document clients still complete the flow, an invalid value closes the routes, a frozen gate passes, the checker reviews, and the head lands on main.","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:5d56adca71ff5f036e167df9b9228468a2f79f13 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0d3d93d0754c6a3eeae515f3c3dc0c10b30d972d, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0f403e804f9757ee6c0664ea9757b53711be3991, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:16d4bcf17e223194b265c810a331c1b9265345b9, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:177f0c558ceeae863608c2a65e6396f8d2b944c9 and 81 more","target_head":"d7f1ebf7b6246a936fa590d6fbe2c24bbb9c18c8","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a23